A record: its fields are read by their names, and changed with with. The function takes an MS and gives the sum of its catch field and the fixed field of the same record after the change.
---

---
type MS = MS {
	st: Int
	fixed: Int
	catch: Int
}
fn m
	let n = with m {
		fixed = 10
	}
	(+ (fixed n) (catch m))
---
MS {
	st = 1
	fixed = 2
	catch = 3
	} => 13 fuel 1000
MS {
	st = 0
	fixed = 0
	catch = 0
	} => 10 fuel 1000
